@@ -18,3 +18,17 @@ resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, "/b");                    // throws JsonPointerError
 Pointer or does not resolve to a value of the document (missing member, out-of-range index, `-`, or a
 token applied to a primitive). `null` and other falsy values resolve normally. Only own members are
 looked up, and the document is never modified.
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar" }, [{ op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }]); // { foo: "bar", baz: "qux" }
+```
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and
+`test` in order and returns the new document. It throws `JsonPatchError` when the patch is malformed or
+an operation fails (including a failed `test`); the result is then discarded. Neither the document nor
+the patch is modified, and the result shares no structure with them. Removing the whole document
+(`remove` with path `""`) is an error.
