@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+## Why
+
+Services need to change stored JSON documents and API payloads with standard patches rather than ad-hoc code. The library already resolves JSON Pointers (RFC 6901); JSON Patch (RFC 6902) builds directly on them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)` exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing the six RFC 6902 §4 operations: `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`.
+- It returns a new document and never mutates the document or the patch passed in.
+- It throws `JsonPatchError` when the patch is malformed (RFC 6902 §3) or when an operation fails (§5).
+- Additive only; no existing export changes behaviour. Not breaking.
+
+Governing standard: RFC 6902 (JSON Patch), with RFC 6901 §3–§4 for pointer syntax and evaluation, and RFC 8259 for JSON values.
+
+Out of scope: JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396), generating a patch by diffing two documents, the `-` array token outside `add`/`copy`/`move` targets, in-place patching, and `application/json-patch+json` media-type handling or parsing of patch text.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 patch to a JSON document, non-mutating, with strict validation and errors.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None. `json-pointer` is unchanged.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new export `applyPatch` and error class `JsonPatchError`.
+- `test/json-patch.test.ts`: new tests; `README.md`: short usage section.
+- No dependencies added.
