+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-18-add-json-patch/specs/json-patch/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,204 @@
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch shape and validation
+Per RFC 6902 §3, a patch SHALL be an array of operation objects. Each operation SHALL have a string `op` member that is one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`, and a string `path` that is a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3). `add`, `replace` and `test` SHALL have a `value` member (any JSON value, including `null`); `move` and `copy` SHALL have a string `from` that is a valid JSON Pointer. Members not defined for the operation SHALL be ignored. Any violation SHALL cause an error to be thrown. An empty patch SHALL return a document equal to the input.
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object, `null`, a string or `undefined`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Operation is not an object
+- **WHEN** an element of the patch is `null`, an array or a primitive
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or unknown op
+- **WHEN** an operation has no `op`, a non-string `op`, or an `op` such as `"merge"` or `"ADD"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid path
+- **WHEN** an operation has no `path`, a non-string `path`, or a path that is not a valid pointer such as `"a"` or `"/a~2"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value
+- **WHEN** an `add`, `replace` or `test` operation has no `value` member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value is a value
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":null}` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":null}`
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid from
+- **WHEN** a `move` or `copy` operation has no `from`, a non-string `from`, or an invalid pointer
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown extra members
+- **WHEN** an operation has an additional member such as `"comment"`
+- **THEN** it is ignored
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** a document equal to the input is returned
+
+### Requirement: Non-mutating and atomic
+Per RFC 6902 §5, if any operation fails the whole patch is in error. `applyPatch` SHALL NOT mutate the document or the patch. The result SHALL NOT share objects or arrays with the document or with the patch's `value` members, so later changes to the result cannot affect them. On error nothing is returned and the inputs remain unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Input document unchanged
+- **WHEN** a patch with several operations is applied
+- **THEN** the original document deep-equals its prior snapshot
+
+#### Scenario: Failure part way
+- **WHEN** the first operation is valid and the second fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Patch values are not aliased
+- **WHEN** an `add` value is an object and the result is later modified
+- **THEN** the patch's `value` is unaffected
+
+### Requirement: add operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.1, `add` SHALL, for an object parent, set the member (replacing it if it exists); for an array parent, insert before the given index, with index equal to the array length or `-` appending; and for the empty path replace the whole document. The parent of the target SHALL exist. An array index SHALL match RFC 6901 §4 (no leading zeros, no sign) and SHALL NOT exceed the array length.
+
+#### Scenario: Add object member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/baz","value":"qux"}` is applied to `{"foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":"bar","baz":"qux"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces existing member
+- **WHEN** `add` targets an existing member
+- **THEN** its value is replaced
+
+#### Scenario: Insert into array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/foo/1","value":"qux"}` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Append to array
+- **WHEN** the path is `/foo/-` or `/foo/2` on a two-element array
+- **THEN** the value is appended
+
+#### Scenario: Array index out of range or malformed
+- **WHEN** the path is `/foo/3` on a two-element array, or `/foo/01`, `/foo/-1`, `/foo/x`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing parent
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a/b/c","value":1}` is applied to `{"a":{}}` or the parent is a primitive
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace whole document
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the result is the value, whatever its type
+
+#### Scenario: Hostile key
+- **WHEN** `add` targets `/__proto__` with value `{"x":1}`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member named `__proto__` and `Object.prototype` is not polluted
+
+### Requirement: remove operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.2, `remove` SHALL delete the target location, which MUST exist. Removing an array element SHALL shift later elements down. Removing the root (`""`) is not defined by the RFC for a non-container result; it SHALL result in an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove object member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/baz"}` is applied to `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":"bar"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/foo/1"}` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** the member does not exist, the index is out of range, or the path is `/foo/-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Remove root
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.3, `replace` SHALL replace the value at the target, which MUST exist. With the empty path the whole document SHALL be replaced.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/baz","value":"boo"}` is applied to `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"baz":"boo","foo":"bar"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace array element
+- **WHEN** `replace` targets `/foo/0` of `{"foo":["a","b"]}`
+- **THEN** only that element changes and the length is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** the member does not exist, the index equals the array length, or the path is `/foo/-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace root
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the result is the value
+
+### Requirement: move operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.4, `move` SHALL remove the value at `from` (which MUST exist) and add it at `path`, as `remove` followed by `add`. `from` MUST NOT be a proper prefix of `path`. Moving a location to itself SHALL leave the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/foo/waldo","path":"/qux/thud"}` is applied to `{"foo":{"bar":"baz","waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":{"bar":"baz"},"qux":{"corge":"grault","thud":"fred"}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/foo/1","path":"/foo/3"}` is applied to `{"foo":["all","grass","cows","eat"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["all","cows","eat","grass"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Missing from
+- **WHEN** `from` does not resolve
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `from` is `/a` and `path` is `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move to itself
+- **WHEN** `from` equals `path` and exists
+- **THEN** the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Move to root
+- **WHEN** `path` is `""` and `from` is `/a`
+- **THEN** the result is the value that was at `from`
+
+### Requirement: copy operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.5, `copy` SHALL add at `path` a deep copy of the value at `from`, which MUST exist, as an `add`. The copy SHALL NOT share structure with the source.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"copy","from":"/foo/waldo","path":"/qux/thud"}` is applied to `{"foo":{"waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** `/qux/thud` is `"fred"` and `/foo/waldo` is still present
+
+#### Scenario: Copy is independent
+- **WHEN** an object is copied and then one copy is changed by a later operation
+- **THEN** the other is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Copy missing source
+- **WHEN** `from` does not resolve
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: test operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.6, `test` SHALL succeed only if the value at `path` (which MUST exist) equals `value`, and otherwise an error SHALL be thrown. Equality: strings compare by code points; numbers by numeric value (`1` equals `1.0`); `null`, `true` and `false` only to themselves; arrays by equal length and element-wise equality in order; objects by the same set of member names with equal values, member order ignored. Values of different types are never equal. `test` does not change the document.
+
+#### Scenario: Test passes
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a/b","value":{"c":[1,2],"d":null}}` is applied to a document where `/a/b` is `{"d":null,"c":[1,2]}`
+- **THEN** it succeeds and the result equals the input
+
+#### Scenario: Test fails on different value
+- **WHEN** the value differs, including `"1"` against `1`, `null` against `0`, `[]` against `{}`, `[1,2]` against `[2,1]`, or an object with an extra member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test on missing path
+- **WHEN** the path does not resolve
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test whole document
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the whole document is compared
+
+#### Scenario: Failed test aborts the patch
+- **WHEN** a `test` fails before later operations
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and no result is returned
+
+### Requirement: Operations apply sequentially
+Per RFC 6902 §3 and §5, operations SHALL be applied in order, each to the result of the previous one.
+
+#### Scenario: Later operation sees earlier result
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":{}}` is followed by `{"op":"add","path":"/a/b","value":1}` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{"b":1}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Error type
+- **WHEN** any validation or operation error occurs
+- **THEN** the error is an instance of `JsonPatchError` (an `Error`)
