+# json-patch Specification
+
+## Purpose
+Lets callers change a JSON document with a standard JSON Patch (RFC 6902): the add, remove, replace, move, copy and test operations are applied in order to produce a new document, failing loudly on invalid patches or failed operations.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch shape and validation
+Per RFC 6902 §3, a patch SHALL be an array of operation objects. Each operation SHALL have a string `op` member that is one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`, and a string `path` that is a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3). `add`, `replace` and `test` SHALL have a `value` member (any JSON value, including `null`); `move` and `copy` SHALL have a string `from` that is a valid JSON Pointer. Members not defined for the operation SHALL be ignored. Any violation SHALL cause an error to be thrown. An empty patch SHALL return a document equal to the input.
+
