+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.3, `replace` SHALL replace the value at the target, which MUST exist. With the empty path the whole document SHALL be replaced.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/baz","value":"boo"}` is applied to `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"baz":"boo","foo":"bar"}`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace array element
+- **WHEN** `replace` targets `/foo/0` of `{"foo":["a","b"]}`
+- **THEN** only that element changes and the length is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** the member does not exist, the index equals the array length, or the path is `/foo/-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace root
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the result is the value
+
+### Requirement: move operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.4, `move` SHALL remove the value at `from` (which MUST exist) and add it at `path`, as `remove` followed by `add`. `from` MUST NOT be a proper prefix of `path`. Moving a location to itself SHALL leave the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/foo/waldo","path":"/qux/thud"}` is applied to `{"foo":{"bar":"baz","waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":{"bar":"baz"},"qux":{"corge":"grault","thud":"fred"}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/foo/1","path":"/foo/3"}` is applied to `{"foo":["all","grass","cows","eat"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["all","cows","eat","grass"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Missing from
+- **WHEN** `from` does not resolve
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `from` is `/a` and `path` is `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move to itself
+- **WHEN** `from` equals `path` and exists
+- **THEN** the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Move to root
+- **WHEN** `path` is `""` and `from` is `/a`
+- **THEN** the result is the value that was at `from`
+
+### Requirement: copy operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.5, `copy` SHALL add at `path` a deep copy of the value at `from`, which MUST exist, as an `add`. The copy SHALL NOT share structure with the source.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"copy","from":"/foo/waldo","path":"/qux/thud"}` is applied to `{"foo":{"waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** `/qux/thud` is `"fred"` and `/foo/waldo` is still present
+
+#### Scenario: Copy is independent
+- **WHEN** an object is copied and then one copy is changed by a later operation
+- **THEN** the other is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Copy missing source
+- **WHEN** `from` does not resolve
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: test operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.6, `test` SHALL succeed only if the value at `path` (which MUST exist) equals `value`, and otherwise an error SHALL be thrown. Equality: strings compare by code points; numbers by numeric value (`1` equals `1.0`); `null`, `true` and `false` only to themselves; arrays by equal length and element-wise equality in order; objects by the same set of member names with equal values, member order ignored. Values of different types are never equal. `test` does not change the document.
+
+#### Scenario: Test passes
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a/b","value":{"c":[1,2],"d":null}}` is applied to a document where `/a/b` is `{"d":null,"c":[1,2]}`
+- **THEN** it succeeds and the result equals the input
+
+#### Scenario: Test fails on different value
+- **WHEN** the value differs, including `"1"` against `1`, `null` against `0`, `[]` against `{}`, `[1,2]` against `[2,1]`, or an object with an extra member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test on missing path
+- **WHEN** the path does not resolve
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test whole document
+- **WHEN** the path is `""`
+- **THEN** the whole document is compared
+
+#### Scenario: Failed test aborts the patch
+- **WHEN** a `test` fails before later operations
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and no result is returned
+
+### Requirement: Operations apply sequentially
+Per RFC 6902 §3 and §5, operations SHALL be applied in order, each to the result of the previous one.
+
+#### Scenario: Later operation sees earlier result
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":{}}` is followed by `{"op":"add","path":"/a/b","value":1}` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{"b":1}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Error type
+- **WHEN** any validation or operation error occurs
+- **THEN** the error is an instance of `JsonPatchError` (an `Error`)
